    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.99.27: a radius where a condition has no informative patient is not tested (adjusted_for \"none (no_information)\")\n\nThe allocation effect is bounded: an image of an avoiding pair with no `to` cell next to a `from` cell has y = -1\nexactly, and one of an attracting pair with every `to` cell next to one +1. When every patient of a condition is at the\nbound, that condition's CR2 variance is exactly 0, the se rests on the other condition's few informative patients and\nthe Satterthwaite df stay at 9-14 (t of -44 to -63 under relabelling). The core's informative_units() counts, per\ncondition, the units with at least one image row whose (O - E) / n is not exactly -1 or +1 (the omni_calib engine's\ndefinition). pair_tests(): allocation, se > 0 and a condition with none -> p and the unadjusted p NaN, with adjustment\ndesign 2 \"no_information\" (no design fitted), and the radius does not enter the davies, maxT or cauchy combination.\nR's .cell_rows_test() does the same, and .cell_pair_test_levels() (more than two conditions) leaves the pair untested\n(reason \"no_information\") when any level has none. The count effect and Kontextual have no bound and are not touched;\nsurvival has no condition groups (a response with no variation is already not tested). The printed summary counts the\npairs not tested; the vignette's checks count BH calls with na.rm = TRUE.\n\nChecks: refs.R 24 of 26 identical() to 1.99.26 (omni_davies_allocation_t40: 156 of 40000 radius tests, all r = 2 on\nthe avoid side, now NA, and the combined p of 131 of 1600 pairs; kontextual$diab/diab_adj: 14 of 193 three-stage\npairs no longer tested, the same 14 that the engine's definition finds); maxt_refs.R 11 of 11 identical; memref.R\nidentical except diabetes (the same 14 pairs). Every count result and Kontextual is identical. On the investigation's\nworst cases (HCC shuffle 14, Metabric 25, Vannan min3 15) and on all 31 labellings of the 12 worst-calibrated real-data\nanalyses, the package's omnibus and single-radius p equa",
    "time": 1792162502
  },
